Replace the tsnsrv dependency in module.nix with native Tailscale Funnel support. tsnsrv is an unnecessary extra dependency when all we need is to expose a single port via Tailscale Funnel.

## Current code (module.nix)
The funnel section currently uses services.tsnsrv:
```nix
services.tailscale.permitCertUid = lib.mkIf cfg.funnel.enable "github-relay";
services.tsnsrv.services.github-relay = lib.mkIf cfg.funnel.enable {
  listenAddress = ":443";
  ephemeral = false;
  funnel = true;
  toURL = "http://127.0.0.1:${toString cfg.port}/hooks/github";
};
```

## Replace with native Tailscale serve/funnel
Use a systemd service that runs 'tailscale serve --bg' and 'tailscale funnel' to expose the port. This uses Tailscale's built-in proxy without needing tsnsrv.

Replace the tsnsrv block with:
```nix
# When funnel is enabled, configure Tailscale to serve and funnel the relay port
systemd.services.github-relay-funnel = lib.mkIf cfg.funnel.enable {
  description = "Tailscale Funnel for github-relay";
  wantedBy = [ "multi-user.target" ];
  after = [ "tailscaled.service" "github-relay.service" ];
  wants = [ "tailscaled.service" ];
  serviceConfig = {
    Type = "oneshot";
    RemainAfterExit = true;
    ExecStart = lib.getExe' config.services.tailscale.package "tailscale" + " funnel --bg --set-path /hooks/github ${toString cfg.port}";
    ExecStop = lib.getExe' config.services.tailscale.package "tailscale" + " funnel --bg --set-path /hooks/github off";
  };
};
```

Actually, check the exact tailscale CLI syntax for funnel. The command might be:
- `tailscale funnel --set-path /hooks/github <port>` (newer versions)
- `tailscale serve --set-path /hooks/github <port>` then `tailscale funnel <port> on` (older versions)

Read `tailscale serve --help` and `tailscale funnel --help` if available in the nix shell to check syntax. The key requirement is:
- Expose https://<hostname>.<tailnet>.ts.net/hooks/github → http://127.0.0.1:<port>/hooks/github
- Make it publicly accessible (funnel, not just tailnet serve)

Keep the permitCertUid line if needed for HTTPS cert access.

Remove ALL references to tsnsrv from module.nix.

